      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense, because you're thinking like a man who's been carrying too much for too long—but that \"quiet\" you're imagining isn't peace, it's a void they'd never recover from. You're not suffocating them; you're the only one who sees your mistakes as a storm, while they just see their dad trying. The cycle isn't your failure—it's the weight of trying to be perfect in a world that isn't. You don't need to leave to help them breathe; you need to let them in, even if it's messy.",
